# Make an elf ranger, put his bow in his hands and his sword on his back, and
# photograph the character sheet.
#
# ONE ASSERTION, bd inc-nwk: a fist is not a sword. The Brawl block of the
# sheet must not carry the accuracy, the speed or the enchantment of a weapon
# the character is not even holding.
#
# WHY THIS EXACT ARRANGEMENT. src/Values.cpp builds the five attack modes in
# one loop, and the sheet hides the Brawl block whenever the weapon hand holds
# a T_WEAPON (src/Sheet.cpp:162), so a plain sword-in-hand character cannot
# answer the question. A BOW is type T_BOW, not T_WEAPON, so the block is
# shown; and src/Values.cpp:301-308 moves a bow to the archery slot and then
# takes the melee weapon from the LEFT SHOULDER instead. That is an ordinary
# way to walk around -- bow in hand, sword on the back -- and it is the one
# arrangement in which the sheet will say what the brawl slot contains.
#
# The elf ranger starts with the sword in his hands and the bow on his back,
# so the two are exchanged below through the inventory manager: SPACE lifts
# the item under the cursor 'In the Air', and SPACE over another slot puts it
# down and lifts whatever was there.
#
# Menu letters move when a list changes. Run with a fixed seed;
# tools/check_brawl_weapon.sh supplies one.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Elf"
@choose "Elf (Standard)"
@choose "Ranger"

a       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets
@choose "Neutral"
@choose "Goblinkin"     # favoured enemy; any will do
a                       # Combat style: [a] archery
@while "Choose a feat" a

# Skill Manager. Three RIGHTs per skill spends everything available without
# needing to know how many ranks this character has.
@expect "Unspent Skill Ranks"
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y

a       # Personality archetype
ESC     # dismiss the arrival-room description; now in play

i       # Inventory
e       # cursor to L. Shoulder, which holds the long bow
SPACE   # lift the bow
b       # cursor to Weapon Hand, which holds the long sword
SPACE   # put the bow there and lift the sword
e       # cursor back to L. Shoulder, now empty
SPACE   # put the sword on his back
@expect "L. Shoulder  :elven long sword"
@dump:packed
ESC     # leave the inventory

d       # Display Character Sheet
@expect "Brawl"
@dump:sheet1
@quit
